From 239784b67338f675a756ca106ff49eb061822c51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Improver <pandemonium-improver@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:19:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] perf(sim): batch entity removal in death & cleanup (stage
 8)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stage 8's death loop removed one entity at a time, each call doing up to
13 binary searches + 13 Vec::remove shifts across the capability stores.
For m simultaneous deaths this was O(m · (log n + n)) per store.

Add World::remove_batch(ids: &[EntityId]) — a single merge-join sweep per
store (both ids and stores are ascending), reducing the cost to O(n + m)
per store. The death loop now marks Lifecycle::Dead, releases footprints,
and emits Died events per-entity, then calls remove_batch once with the
dead-id slice.

The post-state is byte-identical to the per-id path — proven by a new
test that builds two identical worlds, removes the same non-contiguous
id set via each path, and asserts every store compares equal. Golden
hashes (determinism, economy, combat, movement, alpha_loop) remain
unchanged: 352 dev tests green.

Cost shape (alpha scale, n=200, m=10 dead): ~27k → ~2.7k ops per store
pass, a ~10x speedup. At the 10x scale test (n=2000, m=100 dead): ~100x.

Aligns with the user's 'better performance' goal and prepares M10's perf
baseline (plan §15) without changing any observable behavior.
---
 crates/sim/src/sim.rs   |  20 ++++--
 crates/sim/src/world.rs | 136 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 150 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

