From 554c9c4137c5c5d2aa475098eb54f1424eb34c00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Improver <pandemonium-improver@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:22:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] perf(sim): lockstep entity_view with health store in
 snapshot/player_view
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sim::snapshot and Sim::player_view both projected each entity to an
EntityView by calling self.entity_view(id), which does a binary search
through the health store for hp_fraction_milli. For n entities that's
n × O(log h) per snapshot, plus another full pass through entities for
the player_view's fog filter.

Replace with entity_views_lockstep — a single forward walk over the
entity iterator and the health store (both ascending by id), peeking
the next health entry to compute hp_fraction_milli in O(n + h). The
output is byte-identical to the per-id path; the per-id entity_view
helper is removed (it was an internal implementation detail with no
remaining callers after the lockstep path replaces it).

player_view still iterates entities twice (the fog filter then the
view projection), but the second pass no longer re-looks-up the
health entry — the lockstep walk skips ahead as the entity stream
filters. The next step (separate commit) trims hud_state's player_view
call entirely, since the HUD only needs the player's ledger.

Golden hashes (determinism, vision, content_pipeline, engine, sim)
unchanged: 352 dev tests green. Cost shape: snapshot() drops from
O(n log n) to O(n) over health lookups — meaningful for the renderer's
per-frame snapshot path and the soak runner's per-tick checkpoint.
---
