From feb0a1ef215d7526c93a8a228da0085c62abb0b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Improver <pandemonium-improver@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:26:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] perf(fx): make Fx::from_milli a const fn
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every operation in from_milli (i64 arithmetic, the as-i32 cast, the
clamp) is const-evaluable in stable Rust 1.98 once the clamp is
written by hand (i64::clamp is not yet const-stable — it requires
Ord to be a const trait).

Marking the fn const lets callers build compile-time constants like
 for table-driven
content stats — useful for future static lookup tables without
paying for the conversion at runtime or wrapping every entry in
once_cell::sync::Lazy.

The behavior is unchanged (same raw output for every input), pinned
by an existing property test plus a new const-context test that
proves the conversion runs at compile time and that the saturation
contract still holds in const context.
---
 crates/fx/src/fixed.rs | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/fx/src/fixed.rs b/crates/fx/src/fixed.rs
index f336c32..e2d1afb 100644
--- a/crates/fx/src/fixed.rs
+++ b/crates/fx/src/fixed.rs
@@ -63,9 +63,23 @@ impl Fx {
     /// Converts thousandths (the plan §10.2 authoring unit — e.g. milli-tiles,
     /// milli-tiles per second), rounding toward zero; saturates outside the
     /// representable range.
-    pub fn from_milli(milli: i32) -> Self {
+    ///
