The camera already had rotate() and set_pitch() methods but no input
bindings. Add the two Generals: Zero-Hour-style controls the plan §11.3
section anticipates ('pan by edge + keys, zoom toward the cursor, optional
rotation'):

- Q / E — orbit the camera left/right around its target, scaled by the
  real frame delta (frame-rate-independent, like the WASD pan). A full
  turn takes ~6 seconds at the default rate. Cancels an armed attack-move
  so the player can re-orient mid-order.
- Ctrl + wheel — tilt the pitch up/down (Generals-style), clamped to the
  supported range. ~12 notches cover the full pitch range. Without Ctrl
  the wheel still zooms toward the cursor (M9.1's behavior, unchanged).

Adds the supporting getters on RtsCamera (pitch, yaw, distance) and an
adjust_pitch(delta) helper that clamps. The yaw/distance getters also
make camera state observable for tests.

The README's controls section now lists Q/E and Ctrl+wheel. No sim-side
changes — the camera is presentation-only (ADR-0001), so golden hashes
are unaffected: 352 dev tests green.
