From 8bcae6f3e6a5fe9104b343d1d37675e628f135c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pandemonium Improver <pandemonium-improver@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:32:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] feat(tools): add soak subcommand for M10 prep (A7
 acceptance gate)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Plan §12 calls for 'tools soak --matches N' to run many seeded AI-vs-AI
matches with crash/stall detection and win-rate telemetry — the A7
acceptance gate (plan §13: '1000 seeded AI-vs-AI matches complete with
no panics, no stuck matches, no invariant violations').

This is the sequential, single-process version: suitable for a developer
machine or a CI step that wants the per-match telemetry the parallel
subprocess version would have to assemble from separate log files.
Nightly CI that wants parallelism can spawn N
`headless --seed N --ticks T --p1 ai --p2 ai` subprocesses and aggregate
their output — the engine's run_command_log re-simulation path is the
same one this runner drives.

Reports:
- matches run, resolved (player 0 wins / player 1 wins), mutual
  destruction, unresolved (A7 stuck signal), crashed (A7 crash signal)
- per-match end ticks: average and max
- resolution rate (A7 wants 100%)
- wall-clock throughput in ticks/second

Exits non-zero only when a match crashed (the 'A7 crash signal' is the
non-zero exit; unresolved matches surface in the report but the runner
completes — the report is the evidence the soak is meant to produce).

Unit tests pin the report aggregation (win/loss/mutual/unresolved
counting, max/avg end tick, resolution rate at zero matches, outcome
label coverage). The CLI is exercised by an end-to-end smoke run; the
default (matches=8, ticks=18000) is sized for local iteration, not for
the A7 1000-match scale (which lives in nightly CI).
